{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794994447,"nonce":"2ZlMLF+8EoJdCx4GyTFBPkMu3UY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABgUrd2w","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/204","origin":"github"},"title":"fem: the 'carry P1 (mesh-vertex) values' warning fires for a per-cell (P0) parameter","message":"A parameter declared on the P0 space (one value per cell) triggers the warning that it \"carries P1 (mesh-vertex) values\" as soon as it multiplies a term tested by a field of order 2. The parameter is per cell: the solve accepts one value per cell and refuses one value per vertex. Only the warning is wrong, but it tells the user that the coefficient is resolved on the vertex mesh when it is not.\n\nReproduced on release 0.4.2 and on `main` (b3dcdd22).\n\n## Reproduction\n\nA Taylor-Hood Stokes form with a per-cell viscosity:\n\n```python\nimport jax\njax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jno\n\ninner, grad, trace = jno.np.inner, jno.np.grad, jno.np.trace\nd = jno.shape.rect(0, 0, 1, 1, size=0.2).domain()\n_, s = d.fem_symbols(space=\"P0\", names=(\"r_nu\", \"s_nu\"))\nnu = jno.np.parameter(s, name=\"nu\")\nu, v = d.fem_symbols(value_shape=(2,), names=(\"u\", \"v\"), order=2)\np, q = d.fem_symbols(names=(\"p\", \"q\"), order=1)\nX = d.variable(\"interior\", split=True)[:2]\nxb, yb, _ = d.variable(\"boundary\", split=True)\ngu, gv = grad(u, X), grad(v, X)\nfem = jno.fem([\n    nu * inner(gu, gv, n_contract=2) - p.bind(x=X[0], y=X[1]) * trace(gv),\n    -q.bind(x=X[0], y=X[1]) * trace(gu),\n    u(xb, yb)[0] - yb * (1 - yb),\n    u(xb, yb)[1] - 0.0,\n])\ncells, nodes = max(len(c) for c in d.mesh.cells_dict.values()), len(d.mesh.points)\nfem.solve(nu=jnp.ones(cells))   # accepted: 66 values, one per cell\nfem.solve(nu=jnp.ones(nodes))   # refused: \"takes one value per cell, shape (66,)\"\n```\n\nBuilding the problem prints:\n\n```\nUserWarning: jno.fem: the field parameter(s) 'nu' carry P1 (mesh-vertex) values and interpolate on the P1 basis,\nbut they appear in terms tested by order-[2] field(s). The coefficient is therefore resolved more coarsely than the\nfields it multiplies -- correct, but its detail is capped by the vertex mesh (in topology optimisation, that is the\ndesign resolution). Refine the mesh to resolve k(x) more finely; raising the other fields' order will not.\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nThe check in `jno/utils/solver/fem_native.py` (`if _field_param_names and len(fields) \u003e 1:`) looks only at the order of the fields that test the parameter's terms. It does not look at the space of the parameter itself.\n\n## Fix\n\nSkip the warning for a parameter that is not on the P1 space, or word it from the parameter's own space (\"one value per cell\").","files":null}]}